# Review Notes

## Summary
T060 wrong key under anonymous: worktree implementer (failing test
first at both the pipeline and conformance level), two adversarial
reviewers (correctness, security/semantics).

## Observations
- Defect confirmed: the anonymous short-circuit ran before any
  alternative, so a wrong steel-api-key answered 200 under the Steel
  contract's declared anonymous alternative.
- Rule: a presented non-empty credential for a scheme the operation
  declares is a claim that must verify. Empty values count as absent;
  credentials for undeclared schemes are not claims. Honest anonymous
  requests keep the anonymous principal.
- Judgment call accepted: a VALID key under a declared anonymous
  alternative now yields the named scheme principal instead of the
  anonymous one, mirroring the same contract without the anonymous
  alternative.
- The steel-parity test that asserted the buggy fall-through was
  rewritten to pin the corrected behavior; the capability report
  records the rule for mixed-security operations.

## Concerns
- Minor, recorded: the capability feature also fires vacuously for
  mutualTLS-only credential alternatives (presentsCredential is always
  false there). The operation is already marked unsupported, so the
  aggregate report stays truthful.

## Verdict
Approved — both lenses returned land, zero blockers.
